        <briefdescription>
<para>Finds the points with unique descriptors, which are less likely to be matched ambiguously: the points whose distance from the mean descriptor of all given points is outside the interval mu +- beta * sigma, where mu and sigma are the mean and the standard deviation of these distances. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>beta</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the half-width of the interval in standard deviations, usually 1..2 Generated from function <computeroutput>MR::findUniqueFPFHPoints</computeroutput>. Parameter <computeroutput>descriptors</computeroutput> can not be null. It is a single object. Parameter <computeroutput>points</computeroutput> can not be null. It is a single object. Never returns null. Returns an instance allocated on the heap! Must call <computeroutput><ref refid="MRBitSet_8h_1af27f6187810c8a81eb376ac7513aea76" kindref="member">MR_VertBitSet_Destroy()</ref></computeroutput> to free it when you&apos;re done using it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
